    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0447" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.91/7–1950</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-07-19">July 19, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Presentation by Madame Pandit of Prime Minister
                    Nehru’s Personal Message of July 19, 1950</p>
                <p>
                    <table>
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell rendition="#top">Participants:</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Her Excellency, Madame Vijayalakshmi
                                Pandit, Ambassador of India.</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. T. N. Kaul, First Secretary,
                                Embassy of India.</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">The Honorable, Dean Acheson, Secretary
                                of State.</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Joseph S. Sparks, SOA
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p>Madame Pandit handed me a note as she came in, saying that she did not wish to
                    detain me long. I thanked her and read the note which was a reply from Prime
                    Minister Jawaharlal Nehru<anchor n="1" xml:id="d325-f1"/> to my message <pb
                        facs="0448" n="428" xml:id="pg428"/> of July 18, 1950, I told Madame Pandit
                    that I very much appreciated her having brought the message to me and assured
                    her that we would continue to give every serious consideration to the problems
                    with which her brother is so actively concerned. I said that there were many
                    grave issues in the world today but that I was confident that they could be
                    resolved by the continued cooperation and determination of likeminded
                    constructive nations such as India and the United States.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d325-f1" n="1" xml:id="d325-f1-content">
                <p>The text of Mr. Nehru’s message is in telegram 148 from New Delhi, received on
                    July 19 at 9:27 a. m., <ref target="#pg425">p. 425</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
